# IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

GOVERNMENT OF SUMENEP REGENCY

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF SUMENEP REGENCY

NUMBER 7 YEAR 2011

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

REGENT OF SUMENEP

Considering:


a. that the number of violence against women and children in Sumenep Regency is still high while services and protection for women and children in Sumenep Regency have not been carried out optimally;
b. that in the framework of implementing regional autonomy, the regulation and service to the community, especially for women and children victims of violence, is the duty and function of the regency government because violence against women and children is a violation of Human Rights;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence in the Regional Regulation of Sumenep Regency.

In View of:







1. Law Number 7 Year 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3277);
2. Law Number 5 year 1998 Concerning Ratification of the Convention Against Torture and Other Cruel, Inhuman or Degrading Treatment or Punishment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1998 Number 164, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3783);
3. Law Number 39 Year 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3886);
4. Law Number 1 Year 2000 concerning ILO Convention number 182 concerning the Prohibition and Immediate Action for the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labor (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2001 Number 30, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3941);
5. Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4235);
6. Law Number 10 Year 2004 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 53, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4389);
7. Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4419);
8. Law Number 32 Year 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 125, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4437), as amended for the second time by Law Number 12 Year 2008 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 59, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4844);
9. Law Number 21 Year 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4720);
10. Government Regulation Number 79 Year 2005 concerning Guidelines for Development and Supervision of Regional Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2005 Number 165, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4593);
11. Government Regulation Number 4 Year 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);
12. Government Regulation Number 38 Year 2007 concerning Division of Government Affairs Between the Government, Provincial Regional Government and Regency/City Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 82, Supplement to State Gazette Number 4737);
13. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 Year 2006 concerning Forms and Types of Regional Legal Products;
14. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 16 Year 2006 concerning Procedures and Preparation of Regional Legal Products;
15. Decree of the Minister of Home Affairs and Regional Autonomy Number 5 Year 2001 concerning Handling of Child Labor;
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection of the Republic of Indonesia Number 01 Year 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) in the field of integrated services for women and children victims of violence.
17. Regional Regulation of East Java Province Number 9 Year 2005 concerning Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence (Regional Gazette of East Java Province Year 2005 Number 4 Series E);
18. Regional Regulation of Sumenep Regency number 4 Year 2003 concerning Community Participation in Government and Development.

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL PEOPLE'S REPRESENTATIVE COUNCIL OF SUMENEP REGENCY

and

REGENT OF SUMENEP

DECIDES:

To Establish:

REGIONAL REGULATION OF SUMENEP REGENCY CONCERNING IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE.

